LICENSE -- DECISION NEEDED (repository owner: Deepinder Singh)
=============================================================

This repository currently has NO licence, which legally means "all rights
reserved": reviewers and artifact evaluators may read it but nobody may reuse,
modify or redistribute it. IEEE TDSC reviewers and ACM/USENIX artifact
evaluation expect an OSI-approved licence and an archived, citable release.
Only the copyright holder(s) can choose; this file is a placeholder so that
the choice is not forgotten. Rename it to LICENSE once decided.

Options (both permissive, both accepted everywhere):

1. MIT
   + shortest, most familiar; maximal reuse.
   - no explicit patent grant; no NOTICE requirement.
   Text: https://opensource.org/license/mit

2. Apache License 2.0   (suggested by the pre-submission review)
   + explicit patent licence and patent-retaliation clause -- relevant for a
     security mechanism that someone might later try to patent around;
   + NOTICE file lets you require attribution of the paper.
   - longer; changed files must carry a modification notice.
   Text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt

Either way, also:
- add a copyright line naming all authors / institutions (check each
  institution's IP policy before release);
- data: the JSONL logs contain AgentDojo task text (AgentDojo is MIT-licensed);
  keep its copyright notice if redistributing the suite text;
- add CITATION.cff and archive the tagged release on Zenodo (DOI), then cite
  the DOI in the paper's "Artifact availability" paragraph.
